WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.799
[moody, intense intro music plays]

01:06.775 --> 01:08.193
[doctor 1] Hello, ma'am.

01:13.907 --> 01:15.492
-Hello there!
-[doctors] Hello, ma'am!

01:15.575 --> 01:17.827
-Hey. Go, Hurry along.
-[doctor 2] Yes, ma'am.

01:17.911 --> 01:19.871
-Enjoy your lunch.
-[doctors] Thank you!

01:19.954 --> 01:21.456
[doctor 2] Have a good day!

01:29.005 --> 01:30.048
[Dong-eun] But, Yeo-jeong,

01:30.924 --> 01:33.218
I'm not looking for a prince now.

01:34.427 --> 01:36.054
Rather than a prince,

01:36.638 --> 01:39.390
I need an executioner with me

01:39.474 --> 01:41.017
who can help me in the hunt.

01:41.101 --> 01:42.102
[indistinct chatter]

01:46.898 --> 01:48.358
[exhales] Thanks so much.

01:48.441 --> 01:51.569
GYODAE CAFE

01:57.325 --> 02:00.495
How is it a lowly fellow
would dare order the director around?

02:00.578 --> 02:03.623
[chuckles] But didn't you have
a nice walk through the park?

02:04.415 --> 02:06.126
-Is that your lunch?
-It's breakfast.

02:06.209 --> 02:08.795
Huh? Ah, come on now. What is this, even?

02:09.295 --> 02:11.464
-I know you're busy, but you have to eat.
-I'm on a diet.

02:11.548 --> 02:13.591
I want to lose four kilograms
and wear a bikini

02:13.675 --> 02:15.510
when I go on my Christmas trip to Guam.

02:15.593 --> 02:18.346
[awkward laughter] Ah, nice.

02:18.429 --> 02:19.264
Thank you.

02:21.933 --> 02:24.227
Mom, I've finally made my decision.

02:24.936 --> 02:26.980
-What?
-I don't wanna teach.

02:27.856 --> 02:28.982
Sure, that's fair.

02:29.816 --> 02:31.192
I want my own practice.

02:31.651 --> 02:32.777
That's great too,

02:32.861 --> 02:35.113
but you just decided that now?

02:35.196 --> 02:36.489
[Yeo-jeong] I knew a while ago.

02:36.573 --> 02:38.741
But I only decided
to tell you about it now.

02:44.956 --> 02:45.790
You're serious?

02:46.374 --> 02:47.208
Yeah, I am.

02:51.129 --> 02:52.213
[sighs]

02:54.174 --> 02:55.175
Good.

02:55.675 --> 02:58.928
Honestly, I'm just happy you didn't
decide to stay in the military forever.

02:59.012 --> 03:00.388
This is a better plan.

03:00.889 --> 03:03.474
Where are you thinking?
Apgujeong? Cheongdam?

03:03.558 --> 03:04.767
Uh, no.

03:04.851 --> 03:05.852
In Semyeong.

03:06.936 --> 03:09.731
The person I'm interested in right now
lives in Semyeong.

03:10.940 --> 03:11.858
You have a girlfriend?

03:11.941 --> 03:14.027
[chuckles] Haven't gotten that far yet.

03:15.653 --> 03:17.280
This is what she's like, Mom.

03:18.156 --> 03:20.325
She's so calm, as if she's a still pond.

03:20.950 --> 03:23.244
But makes me feel like I'm in a storm.

03:24.412 --> 03:25.246
Does she fish?

03:25.330 --> 03:26.539
It's a metaphor, Mom.

03:26.623 --> 03:28.249
So, you're not doing this for money,

03:28.333 --> 03:30.585
or to help out
a medically underprivileged region.

03:30.668 --> 03:31.669
It's for a girl?

03:32.754 --> 03:36.216
-You write all that on your little letter?
-Oh, God.

03:36.299 --> 03:37.425
I'll write a new one, okay?

03:38.259 --> 03:39.302
-[grunts]
-Ow!

03:39.385 --> 03:40.720
You're embarrassing, you know?

03:41.596 --> 03:42.847
Are you sure you just eat salad?

03:48.353 --> 03:51.231
[Dong-eun] Once upon a time,
I believed in all the gods.

03:51.314 --> 03:52.899
[mysterious music playing]

03:52.982 --> 03:55.026
I kneeled in front of them,

03:55.610 --> 03:57.153
praying for salvation.

03:58.488 --> 04:01.199
I was like a patient
with a terminal illness,

04:01.282 --> 04:03.493
latching onto the smallest bit of hope.

04:04.661 --> 04:06.537
I wonder where you are right now

04:06.621 --> 04:08.081
and what you're praying for.

04:08.831 --> 04:10.875
[mysterious music continuing]

04:17.006 --> 04:20.009
[mother] Sew this into Ye-sol's bag
where she won't be able to see it.

04:20.093 --> 04:22.512
Make sure no one touches it.
Do it yourself.

04:23.721 --> 04:24.722
Thank you, Mom.

04:25.431 --> 04:26.557
Did you just find out…

04:28.351 --> 04:30.687
Ye-sol's homeroom teacher

04:30.770 --> 04:31.771
is that bitch?

04:33.398 --> 04:36.317
You're so incompetent. [disappointed sigh]

04:36.401 --> 04:38.403
You should just go home.

04:39.195 --> 04:40.530
I'll take care of this myself.

04:40.613 --> 04:44.033
Whose son-in-law is it
that works in the Ministry of Education?

04:44.117 --> 04:45.285
Oh, stop that.

04:45.368 --> 04:49.372
What if you provoke her, and that bitch
starts to tell people what happened?

04:49.455 --> 04:51.541
What if everybody that I know finds out?

04:53.042 --> 04:54.252
I'm so scared, Mom.

04:54.335 --> 04:56.212
Why are you so scared
of a nobody like her?

04:56.296 --> 04:59.549
It's not her that I'm scared of.
I'm just scared for Ye-sol.

04:59.632 --> 05:01.926
If everyone finds out, Ye-sol will, too.

05:03.428 --> 05:06.973
She might not understand now,
but what if she grows up and finds out?

05:08.391 --> 05:09.517
I'm terrified of that.

05:12.270 --> 05:13.271
Yeon-jin.

05:15.189 --> 05:16.190
Look at me.

05:18.067 --> 05:19.694
Remember what I told you before?

05:20.778 --> 05:21.821
Never look back.

05:23.031 --> 05:24.949
You won't find solutions in the past.

05:25.783 --> 05:27.410
They're always in front of you.

05:28.786 --> 05:31.289
That's just what life is like.

05:32.749 --> 05:33.791
Got it?

05:36.461 --> 05:37.462
[chuckles]

05:38.296 --> 05:40.298
[suspenseful music playing]

05:45.720 --> 05:48.139
[startup notification chiming]

05:54.312 --> 05:57.607
OCTOBER 31ST - NOVEMBER 6TH
FLIGHT SCHEDULE

05:59.650 --> 06:01.611
[Dong-eun] That's when I realized

06:02.111 --> 06:03.446
that God doesn't exist.

06:04.030 --> 06:05.365
We're all just pretending.

06:07.367 --> 06:08.534
So, you know what?

06:09.827 --> 06:11.954
You should pray to me, Yeon-jin.

06:12.038 --> 06:13.831
[menacing music playing]

06:13.915 --> 06:17.210
I'm your only chance for salvation.

06:20.046 --> 06:21.964
[teacher] Wow, he's a handsome guy.

06:23.424 --> 06:24.509
Who's that?

06:24.592 --> 06:25.593
Boyfriend?

06:27.220 --> 06:29.138
-Can you get us coffee, Mr. Kang?
-[Mr. Kang] Huh?

06:31.224 --> 06:33.768
-Oh, sure.
-I don't need a coffee.

06:34.352 --> 06:35.353
I don't mind.

06:38.147 --> 06:41.025
That's exactly your problem.
You only know when we tell you.

06:42.777 --> 06:44.946
Is there something
you want to talk to me about, Mr. Chu?

06:45.029 --> 06:47.615
No, not at all.
I've heard you're a great teacher.

06:48.533 --> 06:50.785
I just want to share
a cup of coffee. [laughs]

06:51.744 --> 06:52.995
[phone vibrating]

06:58.876 --> 06:59.836
MS. KANG

06:59.919 --> 07:02.255
[Hyeon-nam]
Please call me, ma'am. It's urgent.

07:03.381 --> 07:05.341
[Mr. Chu] Is your boyfriend good to you?

07:06.801 --> 07:08.553
I bet he is, right? [chuckles]

07:09.178 --> 07:10.888
I dunno why, but I just assumed

07:10.972 --> 07:13.641
that you'd be into older men,
instead of some young boyfriend.

07:13.724 --> 07:16.352
[gasps] Oh, unless you have both?

07:19.063 --> 07:20.189
[singsong] Kidding.

07:20.273 --> 07:21.732
[laughs]

07:23.151 --> 07:26.070
-Do you have a girlfriend?
-Do I look like I have one?

07:26.154 --> 07:27.113
You really don't.

07:28.239 --> 07:29.449
Why?

07:29.532 --> 07:30.908
Oh, has nobody told you?

07:32.076 --> 07:33.870
Well, I won't say anything.

07:35.788 --> 07:38.833
I can just tell, you're very talented

07:40.084 --> 07:41.627
at saying things that piss people off.

07:41.711 --> 07:43.838
Just like you and creeping people out.

07:43.921 --> 07:44.755
Huh?

07:46.883 --> 07:48.259
Seriously, Ms. Moon.

07:48.968 --> 07:51.888
You should be very thankful right now
that you're a woman.

07:52.430 --> 07:55.349
Because if you were a man,
I would have smacked you.

07:55.433 --> 07:56.434
Oh, really?

07:57.810 --> 08:00.605
Well, you do look like
somebody who only fights women.

08:05.318 --> 08:06.527
[chuckles]

08:06.611 --> 08:07.778
[singsong] I'm only kidding.

08:09.030 --> 08:11.157
You sounded cute
when you said that before,

08:11.240 --> 08:12.366
so I wanted to try it.

08:19.540 --> 08:21.542
[gentle, mysterious music playing]

08:23.377 --> 08:25.421
[Hyeon-nam] I'm not sure
where Son Myeong-o…

08:25.963 --> 08:28.966
I've lost him a few times before,
when he rides his bike,

08:29.675 --> 08:32.512
but I could usually always find him

08:32.595 --> 08:34.388
by watching his apartment
for a few days or so.

08:34.472 --> 08:36.933
But after this day,
he hasn't been home or at the club.

08:38.976 --> 08:41.187
You last saw him
at the travel agency here?

08:41.270 --> 08:42.271
Yeah.

08:43.397 --> 08:45.775
What if he's back on their side now?

08:45.858 --> 08:46.859
For money, you know?

08:46.943 --> 08:49.320
[sighs] Since he got
the plane ticket that day,

08:49.403 --> 08:52.156
and then he just left the country
the very next day.

08:53.908 --> 08:55.576
I'll check out the travel agency.

08:59.330 --> 09:00.581
Wait until the weekend.

09:00.665 --> 09:01.791
See what happens.

09:01.874 --> 09:02.708
Right.

09:03.251 --> 09:06.754
Unless he's been murdered,
it's not really in our best interest

09:06.837 --> 09:08.214
to disclose that he's gone missing.

09:08.297 --> 09:11.551
If he's actually been murdered,
you say? What?

09:12.051 --> 09:13.052
[gasps]

09:14.428 --> 09:16.889
So, you really think
he might already be dead?

09:16.973 --> 09:18.724
It's definitely possible.

09:19.642 --> 09:21.018
-I'll contact you.
-Hold on!

09:21.686 --> 09:23.479
Um, did you…

09:25.648 --> 09:26.482
by any chance

09:28.568 --> 09:29.443
do that to him?

09:30.444 --> 09:32.071
You're asking if I killed him?

09:32.154 --> 09:32.989
Son Myeong-o?

09:33.614 --> 09:36.117
If you did, seriously,

09:36.200 --> 09:39.579
then I should know about it,
so I can prepare for whatever occurs.

09:39.662 --> 09:40.663
No, you don't.

09:41.330 --> 09:43.833
Even if I did,
you don't need to know about it.

09:45.167 --> 09:46.002
What?

09:46.085 --> 09:49.171
The deal that you and I made
at the beginning is a simple one.

09:50.339 --> 09:53.593
You do what I ask you to do,
and I do what you ask of me.

09:54.218 --> 09:55.761
That's all we need to do for each other.

09:58.014 --> 09:58.848
You and I,

10:00.057 --> 10:01.559
we've gotten too close, ma'am.

10:04.937 --> 10:05.938
[door opens]

10:15.197 --> 10:17.074
[car beeping]

10:19.243 --> 10:21.245
[gentle, mysterious music playing]

10:22.121 --> 10:24.123
[engine turns over]

10:28.836 --> 10:31.005
-[barking]
-[door beeping, opening]

10:33.257 --> 10:34.842
[Jae-jun] Dad's home, Louis.

10:34.925 --> 10:35.926
[sighs]

10:37.053 --> 10:40.139
I haven't been home in a really long time.

10:40.640 --> 10:42.391
I know. I'm sorry.

10:43.309 --> 10:44.435
[grunts]

10:51.609 --> 10:53.819
What? Louis!

10:54.570 --> 10:56.030
Oh, shit.

10:59.367 --> 11:01.035
Why are you doing that, huh?

11:02.536 --> 11:05.039
[sighs] I just apologized, didn't I?

11:06.666 --> 11:08.876
So you're mad because I haven't been home.

11:12.838 --> 11:13.839
What is this?

11:17.259 --> 11:18.678
[menacing music plays]

11:18.761 --> 11:19.762
[grunts]

11:25.935 --> 11:26.811
Oh, shit.

11:28.104 --> 11:29.313
What the fuck?

11:31.691 --> 11:33.609
Motherfucker, where the hell are you?

11:34.193 --> 11:35.861
Guess that fucker was right here.

11:36.570 --> 11:38.280
God, that son of a bitch.

11:38.364 --> 11:39.990
-[Louis whimpers]
-No, not you.

11:42.910 --> 11:43.911
By the way, Louis…

11:46.789 --> 11:48.165
what did you do when he did this?

11:48.749 --> 11:49.875
Did you bite him?

11:49.959 --> 11:55.089
If you just watched it happen,
I'll be really… disappointed.

11:55.172 --> 11:57.758
[menacing music continues]

11:57.842 --> 12:00.219
VIEWERS REPORT PAGE
YOUR REPORT BECOMES OUR NEWS

12:05.975 --> 12:07.643
SCHOOL VIOLENCE

12:10.521 --> 12:12.189
NO POSTS FOUND

12:14.066 --> 12:16.235
[woman 1] How can she expect people
to take her seriously

12:16.318 --> 12:18.028
when she can't even write her own scripts?

12:18.112 --> 12:19.405
Even newbies write their scripts.

12:19.488 --> 12:22.158
[woman 2] We have
another Jaepyeong Construction ad.

12:24.493 --> 12:25.327
Su-mi?

12:27.163 --> 12:29.331
Oh, what? Did you hear that?

12:29.415 --> 12:30.958
Well, you said it pretty loud.

12:31.041 --> 12:34.295
Well, they do say that truth is
louder in your ears, Yeon-jin.

12:34.795 --> 12:36.547
[laughs heartily]

12:37.840 --> 12:40.176
Hey, is this The Newsroom?
[continues laughing]

12:41.051 --> 12:42.094
Su-mi.

12:42.178 --> 12:44.472
You should listen
to our friend over there.

12:44.972 --> 12:47.391
She just said
that my husband gave us another ad.

12:47.892 --> 12:49.435
Don't you understand what that means?

12:49.518 --> 12:53.773
This little station only pays me
2.2 million won a month,

12:53.856 --> 12:58.694
but my husband is giving this place
220 million won, understand?

12:59.195 --> 13:00.863
I know that you're young.

13:00.946 --> 13:02.615
But how long will that last you?

13:02.698 --> 13:04.533
Until next year?
Or maybe the year after that?

13:04.617 --> 13:06.535
Oh my God, you little--

13:06.619 --> 13:09.830
I'm saying that no matter
how much fucking collagen that you use,

13:10.790 --> 13:13.000
you will never be able to be like me.

13:14.043 --> 13:15.377
You're just a young bitch.

13:15.461 --> 13:16.462
[groans]

13:16.545 --> 13:18.380
So, listen, Su-mi,

13:18.464 --> 13:21.091
I can convince them
not to renew your contract,

13:21.175 --> 13:23.135
so don't tempt me, all right?

13:30.267 --> 13:31.435
Please enjoy your meal.

13:32.895 --> 13:33.896
What about Dong-eun?

13:35.189 --> 13:36.106
Still nothing?

13:39.068 --> 13:43.155
Finding someone's private information,
it's not as easy as you might be thinking.

13:44.281 --> 13:47.409
Pulling up info requires
piggybacking onto other cases.

13:49.161 --> 13:50.538
[phone ringing]

13:51.288 --> 13:52.122
JAE-JUN

13:53.249 --> 13:55.167
If it were easy, I'd do it.

14:00.548 --> 14:02.466
You know, the world has changed.

14:02.967 --> 14:04.969
It's not the same world as 18 years ago.

14:05.052 --> 14:08.305
That's why I'm not paying you
the amount I did 18 years ago.

14:10.307 --> 14:13.060
I heard you own a motel,
under your sister's name.

14:14.520 --> 14:15.479
A lot of customers?

14:18.941 --> 14:20.067
Thank you for asking.

14:20.943 --> 14:22.403
I meant to condescend.

14:23.654 --> 14:26.866
I've put some men on it.
I'll let you know when I get something.

14:28.409 --> 14:31.453
You seem way too busy, you know that?

14:35.416 --> 14:36.625
Thanks for your concern.

14:38.002 --> 14:39.712
[Seong-hee] I checked Myeong-o's ticket.

14:41.463 --> 14:45.092
He bought a one-way ticket
for Vladivostok, and nothing else.

14:45.676 --> 14:49.054
Then he didn't even board the flight
he got the one-way ticket for.

14:49.138 --> 14:52.683
And I checked the hotel he reserved too,
but it looks like a no-show.

14:54.226 --> 14:56.520
So he definitely didn't leave the country.

14:56.604 --> 14:57.563
[Seong-hee] Right.

14:57.646 --> 15:00.107
So, why'd you ask about him?
Is something wrong?

15:00.941 --> 15:02.067
Yeah.

15:02.568 --> 15:05.237
I'm not sure if the guy's just missing,

15:05.321 --> 15:07.948
or if I need to go get ready
for his funeral.

15:09.867 --> 15:12.494
I mean, you do have
a lot of black clothes.

15:13.954 --> 15:16.123
[chuckles dryly] Yeah. I do.

15:16.749 --> 15:17.750
[chuckles]

15:19.084 --> 15:21.587
[Dong-eun] Guess Myeong-o
has been snapped in half.

15:22.338 --> 15:25.174
Well, SD cards are expendable anyway.

15:25.799 --> 15:27.801
[mysterious music playing]

15:29.053 --> 15:30.054
Now, I think

15:30.721 --> 15:34.224
I'll have to look for a real butterfly
that'll flap its wings for me.

15:42.441 --> 15:44.818
And I know a butterfly with silk wings

15:44.902 --> 15:46.236
that will help me

15:46.320 --> 15:48.447
brew up a hurricane, Yeon-jin.

15:49.949 --> 15:51.951
[dramatic music playing]

15:59.583 --> 16:02.544
[worker] The wires are all done!
Let's light them up now!

16:04.797 --> 16:06.006
[lights tinkling]

16:07.841 --> 16:08.968
[crowd murmurs, claps]

16:09.051 --> 16:11.845
-[overlapping chatter]
-[man] Great work, everyone.

16:14.765 --> 16:16.892
[man] We thank you on behalf of the city.

16:16.976 --> 16:20.145
Thank you for staying so late here, sir.
We truly appreciate it.

16:20.229 --> 16:21.981
Honestly, I would call it early, not late.

16:22.064 --> 16:23.983
Oh, yes, that's true. [man chuckles]

16:25.859 --> 16:26.944
Great work with this.

16:27.861 --> 16:30.406
I want to commemorate this
and look around.

16:30.489 --> 16:31.573
[man] Yes, of course.

16:33.283 --> 16:35.285
[mysterious music playing]

17:25.919 --> 17:26.837
[music trails off]

17:27.588 --> 17:28.589
[Sa-ra sighs]

17:30.841 --> 17:32.551
[Sa-ra] Fuck, Myeong-o, come on.

17:35.929 --> 17:37.639
I'm out of ice and grass now.

17:40.225 --> 17:41.894
[Myeong-o] Where are you? Can we meet?

17:42.394 --> 17:43.395
Want to come over?

17:43.479 --> 17:44.980
You wanna see me alone?

17:45.064 --> 17:46.065
Why?

17:49.026 --> 17:51.653
[Sa-ra] Come on, read my text.
Fucking read it.

17:54.907 --> 17:56.909
[panicked grunting]

18:07.586 --> 18:09.254
[Hye-jeong] Which ring looks better?

18:09.338 --> 18:11.423
[Jae-jun] The asshole
didn't come to work again today.

18:11.507 --> 18:12.925
And he stole my clothes and watches.

18:13.008 --> 18:16.637
Can you pick one out of these three?
[Hye-jeong gasps] Oh wow, really?

18:16.720 --> 18:18.972
-Which watches?
-[Sa-ra] Hey, I paid you in advance.

18:19.556 --> 18:21.475
I don't care
that you did something stupid.

18:21.558 --> 18:22.559
Business is business.

18:24.436 --> 18:27.815
[suspenseful music continues]

18:30.776 --> 18:31.693
[music trails off]

18:36.240 --> 18:38.325
Would you like to look at another design?

18:38.408 --> 18:39.827
This stone might be too big.

18:39.910 --> 18:41.870
It could be uncomfortable
when you wear it.

18:42.913 --> 18:43.914
No way.

18:44.748 --> 18:46.583
I vastly prefer the big ones.

18:47.459 --> 18:50.379
I like everything big, you know?

18:55.926 --> 18:57.386
Tae-uk, hi! [laughs]

18:57.469 --> 18:59.680
You're early!
I thought you were going to be late.

18:59.763 --> 19:02.391
I haven't managed to pick one out,
because they're so pretty.

19:02.891 --> 19:04.143
Five minutes, please.

19:15.612 --> 19:18.532
Yo, didn't I tell you
to wear high heels around me?

19:19.324 --> 19:21.451
You know I like it when you look tall.

19:21.535 --> 19:24.580
Even if you wear flats,
I won't look taller than you.

19:24.663 --> 19:26.540
Are you really
that embarrassed of my height

19:26.623 --> 19:29.084
No, my legs just hurt because of work.

19:29.168 --> 19:31.587
-[Tae-uk scoffs]
-I'll wear heels next time.

19:32.713 --> 19:33.964
I'm not going to propose.

19:34.047 --> 19:36.800
You just want a bigger stone
than your friends, don't you?

19:37.301 --> 19:39.303
Here. That's the biggest one.

19:39.386 --> 19:40.220
[exclaims]

19:41.763 --> 19:44.183
-Really? Wow!
-[scoffs]

19:44.266 --> 19:46.935
Oh, I love it!
God, it is bigger than the one she has!

19:49.062 --> 19:50.063
Oh, also,

19:50.772 --> 19:52.357
my mom wanted me to tell you.

19:53.025 --> 19:55.110
Don't suggest eating meat to her, okay?

19:55.194 --> 19:57.154
She's vegetarian, you hear me? Hmm?

19:57.654 --> 20:01.950
Yeah, I know. I don't like
eating meat that much, either.

20:02.534 --> 20:03.535
[exclaims happily]

20:06.330 --> 20:08.332
[phone ringing]

20:10.292 --> 20:11.126
[beeps]

20:11.710 --> 20:14.838
[Hyeon-nam] Change directions!
Someone's following your car!

20:14.922 --> 20:16.256
They're right behind you!

20:17.382 --> 20:18.634
[tires screeching]

20:18.717 --> 20:20.636
[intense, ominous music playing]

20:22.429 --> 20:25.724
-What are you doing driving behind me?
-Listen, that's not important right now!

20:26.391 --> 20:28.602
Ugh, I've been doing this every day,

20:28.685 --> 20:31.355
and I never considered
they might send someone to follow us.

20:31.438 --> 20:34.066
I'll just… I'll find a way
to lose them, okay?

20:34.149 --> 20:35.567
No, I'll do it.

20:35.651 --> 20:37.486
Make sure they don't notice you.

20:38.028 --> 20:38.946
[phone beeps]

20:50.832 --> 20:51.667
Huh?

20:53.961 --> 20:56.004
[intense music continuing]

21:34.001 --> 21:35.002
[thud]

21:35.085 --> 21:36.003
[music trails off]

21:44.011 --> 21:45.012
[driver sighs]

21:51.101 --> 21:52.019
You have a death wish?

21:52.602 --> 21:54.563
What the hell were you doing
with your brakes?

21:54.646 --> 21:56.648
I'm sorry about this. Are you guys hurt?

21:56.732 --> 21:59.192
Oh, my back. Ugh, my neck.

21:59.276 --> 22:01.278
What are you gonna fucking do now?

22:01.361 --> 22:02.696
[driver] We're pretty busy people.

22:02.779 --> 22:05.866
So, make your choice between
calling the cops or paying me in cash.

22:05.949 --> 22:07.868
I think you gave me the wrong options.

22:08.368 --> 22:11.288
You're supposed to call
your insurance now, not the police.

22:12.497 --> 22:14.458
If it's a rental car,
call where you rented it.

22:18.086 --> 22:20.213
Fucking shit. Well, aren't you smart.

22:20.297 --> 22:21.340
[frustrated groan]

22:21.923 --> 22:23.967
This is my favorite rental car, okay?

22:26.678 --> 22:28.305
And since you caused the crash,

22:29.264 --> 22:31.016
you should call the cops,

22:31.099 --> 22:33.060
or just give me some fucking cash now.

22:34.269 --> 22:35.520
'Cause this is crazy.

22:36.021 --> 22:39.566
I'm getting scolded on the street,
next to my broken car.

22:40.442 --> 22:42.861
Since we're both busy,
let's do this in cash.

22:43.403 --> 22:44.446
What's your bank number?

22:44.529 --> 22:47.115
That'd be a deposit.
I want you to give me cash.

22:50.952 --> 22:52.329
Give me your phone number.

23:02.047 --> 23:04.049
-[line ringing]
-[phone ringing]

23:08.178 --> 23:11.056
Meet me with cash when I call you.

23:15.310 --> 23:16.311
[door opens]

23:16.812 --> 23:18.355
-[door closes]
-[engine turns over]

23:28.073 --> 23:29.074
[panting]

23:49.386 --> 23:50.512
[gasps]

24:04.818 --> 24:07.195
Did you get hurt anywhere? Let me see.

24:09.448 --> 24:12.159
Weren't you following Jung Jae-jun today?

24:12.242 --> 24:14.035
So why were you driving behind me?

24:14.703 --> 24:17.164
Why did you follow me, then?

24:18.707 --> 24:20.834
I mean, why would I be following you?

24:24.754 --> 24:27.174
Are you suspicious of me right now?

24:30.010 --> 24:31.386
I'm just being careful.

24:32.387 --> 24:33.555
Aren't you nervous too?

24:34.181 --> 24:37.809
I could go to your husband now
and tell him you asked me to kill him.

24:38.393 --> 24:40.770
I could just tell him
everything, whenever.

24:40.854 --> 24:42.689
I'm sure you must have thought about that.

24:48.987 --> 24:51.656
I saw Jae-jun
in front of the school where you work.

24:52.157 --> 24:53.408
He was watching Ye-sol.

24:54.326 --> 24:57.245
So, I happened to be there
because I was following him.

24:57.329 --> 24:58.872
And then I saw you drive by.

24:59.581 --> 25:02.667
I was so happy. Then I saw those people.

25:06.213 --> 25:09.466
I guess that I could worry about all that.

25:11.676 --> 25:14.221
But I wasn't thinking about that at all.

25:14.721 --> 25:15.722
I really wasn't.

25:16.640 --> 25:18.433
I was too busy with the camera,

25:18.517 --> 25:20.685
and then too busy focusing on driving.

25:21.478 --> 25:22.479
[Hyeon-nam sighs]

25:24.856 --> 25:25.815
Get out with me.

25:34.991 --> 25:36.618
-[sighs]
-[door opens]

25:47.337 --> 25:50.590
The restaurant that Jae-jun
goes to often is inside the market.

25:51.091 --> 25:52.592
I got cabbage and made kimchi.

25:52.676 --> 25:54.094
[gentle, kind music playing]

25:54.177 --> 25:55.011
Eat it soon.

25:55.679 --> 25:57.597
I've been carrying it around.

25:59.683 --> 26:01.059
And, if you think about it,

26:01.726 --> 26:04.646
I could spill your secrets
to a lot more people, okay?

26:05.564 --> 26:07.691
Park Yeon-jin, Jeon Jae-jun, Lee Sa-ra.

26:09.734 --> 26:13.530
I was happy buying those cabbages.

26:14.489 --> 26:16.533
I started to dream, since we've met.

26:18.577 --> 26:20.787
Dreaming about dinner with Seon-a…

26:24.291 --> 26:26.001
[sniffling, crying]

26:26.501 --> 26:28.920
And not a dinner
where you just scarf down your food.

26:30.839 --> 26:34.593
But a proper dinner, with stew and eggs,

26:35.510 --> 26:37.304
where you eat as slow as you want.

26:39.139 --> 26:41.600
That kind of dinner is my dream.

26:44.019 --> 26:46.146
I get so happy thinking about it.

26:47.230 --> 26:49.232
[tense music playing]

26:53.111 --> 26:55.280
So you still have other thoughts, then?

26:56.197 --> 26:57.198
Hmm?

26:59.409 --> 27:01.328
Oh. I guess.

27:01.828 --> 27:03.204
[laughing]

27:06.458 --> 27:07.459
Oh.

27:08.627 --> 27:09.628
I'm sorry.

27:10.795 --> 27:12.797
Oh, why am I like this?

27:15.800 --> 27:17.260
Because you're a good person.

27:25.393 --> 27:27.312
That was my fault. I'm sorry.

27:29.064 --> 27:31.399
Your dream will come true.

27:33.526 --> 27:35.904
And you're so kind,
but I can't take the kimchi.

27:43.036 --> 27:44.704
[engine turns over]

27:44.788 --> 27:47.666
[Dong-eun] The two of us
mostly call each other "ma'am."

27:47.749 --> 27:49.084
We're still so distant.

27:51.336 --> 27:53.254
But what else would we call each other

27:53.963 --> 27:55.840
as we plot people's deaths together?

27:55.924 --> 27:57.801
[bell clanking]

27:59.761 --> 28:01.721
We know everything about the darkness

28:02.681 --> 28:04.766
that we plan to unleash, Yeon-jin.

28:06.059 --> 28:08.228
We know how dark it'll be in the end.

28:08.311 --> 28:09.604
[music trails off]

28:09.688 --> 28:10.689
[line ringing]

28:13.400 --> 28:16.611
[operator] The person
you're trying to reach is not available…

28:16.695 --> 28:20.031
Is Yeon-jin not picking up?
Myeong-o's not answering, either.

28:21.366 --> 28:22.909
Maybe they're together somewhere.

28:25.328 --> 28:27.997
You don't know if you're the only guy
Yeon-jin's sleeping with.

28:28.081 --> 28:29.874
Watch your fucking mouth, okay?

28:29.958 --> 28:34.003
I'm just saying,
neither of them is answering their phones.

28:34.462 --> 28:36.214
-But whatever.
-Hye-jeong.

28:39.634 --> 28:41.845
If you want to be a bitch,
then do it right.

28:44.013 --> 28:46.141
You want to be
a successful bitch, don't you?

28:46.641 --> 28:48.101
You're so sloppy.

28:50.186 --> 28:51.020
[sighs]

28:52.856 --> 28:55.233
I have to go now. I have a flight.

29:02.323 --> 29:05.326
Hey, you know Yeon-jin's daughter?

29:07.078 --> 29:08.538
-Ye-sol?
-What about her?

29:12.709 --> 29:13.877
Aren't those Yeon-jin's heels?

29:14.377 --> 29:18.465
I bought them for a flight to London.
I didn't know that she also had them.

29:18.548 --> 29:19.382
What about Ye-sol?

29:20.425 --> 29:21.634
Know when her birthday is?

29:22.427 --> 29:23.428
Ye-sol's birthday?

29:23.511 --> 29:24.679
Do you know or not?

29:24.763 --> 29:26.389
I don't know her exact birthday,

29:27.682 --> 29:30.810
but I know Yeon-jin's mother
set a date for her when she got pregnant,

29:30.894 --> 29:32.145
sometime before Chuseok.

29:32.937 --> 29:34.481
She thought it would bring wealth.

29:34.981 --> 29:36.149
Why do you care now?

29:36.858 --> 29:37.859
Huh.

29:40.236 --> 29:42.572
I wonder if she's my daughter.

29:43.156 --> 29:44.407
Man, you're insane!

29:44.491 --> 29:45.492
[chuckles dryly]

29:46.451 --> 29:48.203
When the sun doesn't sink
below the horizon

29:48.286 --> 29:49.537
in the middle of the summer,

29:49.621 --> 29:52.040
in certain places,
it makes the nights look as bright as day.

29:52.123 --> 29:53.124
It's called a white night.

29:53.208 --> 29:54.042
Yeah, that's right.

29:54.125 --> 29:56.044
It makes it bright all day and night.

29:56.127 --> 29:59.506
Did you know that during white nights,
on the opposite hemisphere,

29:59.589 --> 30:02.550
people have to endure a "polar night"
where it stays dark all day?

30:03.259 --> 30:05.428
I would hate it
if nights lasted that long.

30:05.512 --> 30:08.765
The reason why they call this
a polar night instead of a dark night

30:08.848 --> 30:12.560
is because the nights are so long,
like the polar opposite of a white night.

30:13.186 --> 30:17.357
So, I ask the listeners, were your nights
white or polar during the past week?

30:17.982 --> 30:21.903
I hope you'll get through any tough times
and polar nights throughout the next week.

30:21.986 --> 30:23.196
I'm Park Yeon-jin.

30:23.279 --> 30:24.614
[Kwang-hee] I'm Kwang-hee.

30:24.697 --> 30:28.076
I'm here with everyone's
favorite forecaster, Park Yeon-jin,

30:28.159 --> 30:29.536
for the show Crazy or Bright.

30:29.619 --> 30:31.496
And we've just heard
some amazing stuff from her!

30:31.579 --> 30:33.289
We'll be back after some ads.

30:48.137 --> 30:50.723
[woman] This location has
a very high ceiling,

30:50.807 --> 30:53.601
and it also has a skylight,
which lets in a lot of sunlight.

30:54.477 --> 30:56.229
And it looks even better at night.

30:58.523 --> 31:00.775
This looks great. I'll take this one.

31:00.859 --> 31:03.528
[landlady] It's newly built,
right near a station.

31:03.611 --> 31:05.572
It's very nice, both day and night.

31:05.655 --> 31:07.615
There's a yoga studio and a gym here.

31:08.449 --> 31:12.120
If people hurt themselves working out,
you'll get some new patients.

31:12.203 --> 31:14.080
Your practice would be perfect here.

31:14.163 --> 31:15.874
What kind of doctor are you?

31:15.957 --> 31:17.917
It'd be perfect
if you were an orthopedic surgeon.

31:18.001 --> 31:19.335
I'm a plastic surgeon.

31:19.419 --> 31:20.753
Even better!

31:20.837 --> 31:24.048
I mean, they can get double-eyelid surgery
after their workout.

31:24.132 --> 31:25.133
[laughs]

31:26.718 --> 31:27.927
I definitely want this place.

31:28.928 --> 31:30.263
You sure you're a doctor?

31:30.972 --> 31:32.140
-What?
-You're so eager,

31:32.223 --> 31:34.058
you might be trying to scam me.

31:34.726 --> 31:36.185
[both laugh]

31:36.769 --> 31:38.897
You're very handsome for a doctor.

31:38.980 --> 31:39.814
Ah.

31:40.690 --> 31:44.402
I don't usually brag about these things,
but my nickname is "Mr. Handsome."

31:45.278 --> 31:47.780
People don't believe
I'm a doctor with this face.

31:47.864 --> 31:49.616
I can't even bring up my Mensa membership,

31:49.699 --> 31:51.993
or that I skipped some grades
back in school.

31:52.076 --> 31:54.370
I liked it better
when you weren't talking.

31:55.914 --> 31:56.915
[landlady laughs]

31:58.207 --> 32:00.168
[assistant] Here's your schedule,
and your mail.

32:00.251 --> 32:02.795
On the very top is
the express delivered one.

32:03.296 --> 32:04.422
What?

32:07.717 --> 32:08.718
Hmm.

32:25.401 --> 32:27.028
SON MYEONG-O

32:27.111 --> 32:29.781
[tense, mysterious music playing]

32:56.557 --> 32:57.934
[line ringing]

33:00.144 --> 33:01.145
PLATINUM CC
SON MYEONG-O

33:02.689 --> 33:06.192
[operator] The person
you're trying to reach is not available…

33:07.485 --> 33:08.778
Who's here, you said?

33:13.700 --> 33:15.159
[Do-yeong] It's been a while.

33:17.787 --> 33:19.038
Around three years?

33:21.457 --> 33:24.794
At the opening of your father-in-law's
new building, I believe.

33:27.088 --> 33:29.007
Doesn't look like you're here to golf.

33:29.757 --> 33:31.634
I'm very curious what brought you here.

33:33.344 --> 33:34.971
I can't reach Mr. Son Myeong-o.

33:36.681 --> 33:38.558
Do you know where he might be now?

33:38.641 --> 33:40.768
Wow, you're looking for him as well?

33:43.438 --> 33:44.856
I can't reach him either.

33:45.648 --> 33:46.858
Why do you want to know?

33:49.986 --> 33:51.863
[tense music continuing]

33:55.158 --> 33:55.992
Want one?

33:56.075 --> 33:57.076
I don't care for it.

33:58.745 --> 34:01.122
Do you know
of any other way I can reach him?

34:03.207 --> 34:06.919
You didn't… tell me
why you're looking for him.

34:07.003 --> 34:08.004
It's private.

34:08.963 --> 34:09.922
Between him and me.

34:10.006 --> 34:11.007
[scoffs]

34:12.216 --> 34:14.677
If you have his address,
names of family members, anything…

34:16.637 --> 34:17.930
You get something from him too?

34:20.349 --> 34:21.476
I bet you did.

34:22.435 --> 34:23.352
What'd you get?

34:24.103 --> 34:25.813
How is he trying to threaten you?

34:26.689 --> 34:28.816
Well, what did you get from him, Mr. Jeon?

34:31.402 --> 34:32.737
This is going nowhere, so…

34:33.237 --> 34:36.783
Whoever finds him first
tells the other, okay?

34:37.909 --> 34:39.994
Don't you think you'll find him first?

34:42.497 --> 34:44.040
He's your friend, after all.

34:44.123 --> 34:45.166
He's not my friend.

34:48.544 --> 34:49.712
He was my lackey.

34:49.796 --> 34:50.755
[Jae-jun chuckles]

34:54.008 --> 34:56.803
Well, I should be going now.

35:11.359 --> 35:13.361
[overlapping chatter]

35:17.532 --> 35:19.700
[operator] The person
you're trying to reach is not available.

35:19.784 --> 35:21.911
Please record your message after the tone.

35:21.994 --> 35:24.122
Hey, Myeong-o, you son of a bitch.

35:24.205 --> 35:27.291
So, I guess I'm not
the only one that you targeted?

35:29.210 --> 35:31.587
What do you have
to threaten Do-yeong with, huh?

35:33.131 --> 35:34.382
Is it some woman, or…

35:35.508 --> 35:36.509
or something else?

35:38.302 --> 35:39.303
[sighs]

35:39.887 --> 35:44.684
If Ye-sol… is the fucking reason
Do-yeong and I are lumped together,

35:47.186 --> 35:49.647
I'm going to murder you,
you pathetic asshole.

35:49.730 --> 35:51.732
[indistinct chatter]

35:59.365 --> 36:00.366
[bell rings]

36:06.622 --> 36:08.624
[indistinct chatter continuing]

36:10.710 --> 36:12.003
[exhales heavily]

36:29.562 --> 36:31.397
[mechanic] You can check out the bumper,

36:31.480 --> 36:34.233
and then pick up your key
and make your payment in the office.

36:34.734 --> 36:36.444
-Thank you so much.
-Sure.

36:47.288 --> 36:48.289
[phone chimes]

36:52.627 --> 36:56.422
[Yeo-jeong] I just realized
that we never properly ended our match.

36:57.506 --> 36:59.300
We haven't counted our houses yet.

37:04.138 --> 37:06.474
[meat sizzling on hot plate]

37:07.934 --> 37:10.353
[young Dong-eun wailing]

37:13.022 --> 37:15.608
[dream-like, unsettling music playing]

37:18.486 --> 37:19.987
[sizzling]

37:20.071 --> 37:21.489
[young bullies laughing]

37:21.572 --> 37:23.032
[music intensifies]

37:27.328 --> 37:29.205
[young Dong-eun screaming]

37:32.833 --> 37:33.876
[grunt echoing]

37:37.713 --> 37:39.131
[breathing heavily]

38:00.069 --> 38:02.154
[young Dong-eun wailing]

38:17.795 --> 38:19.297
-What's happening?
-What's going on?

38:19.380 --> 38:21.757
[mechanic 2] Are you okay?
Is something wrong? Can we help?

38:22.258 --> 38:23.259
Excuse me.

38:27.680 --> 38:28.681
Are you okay, ma'am?

38:30.224 --> 38:32.226
[menacing music builds]

38:33.477 --> 38:34.478
[doorbell rings]

38:43.321 --> 38:44.155
What?

38:46.657 --> 38:47.658
Come inside.

38:54.582 --> 38:56.334
Are you sick? What happened?

38:58.711 --> 38:59.587
Just come in.

39:05.926 --> 39:08.054
I don't have all of my furniture yet.

39:08.137 --> 39:11.474
Uh… let me get you some water.
You can sit here.

39:13.059 --> 39:14.643
[Dong-eun] What is this place?

39:20.941 --> 39:21.942
What's going on?

39:22.485 --> 39:24.070
Did I reach out at a bad time?

39:26.364 --> 39:27.615
Did you move here?

39:27.698 --> 39:29.200
My friend works out here,

39:29.283 --> 39:32.411
and he's making a ton of money,
so I came out here to practice, too.

39:32.495 --> 39:34.330
At least,
that's what I planned on telling you.

39:34.413 --> 39:36.415
[awkward laughter] Is it working?

39:39.418 --> 39:40.878
You want to count houses?

39:41.921 --> 39:43.839
I don't want to lose without a reason.

39:45.508 --> 39:47.176
I had a feeling that'd make you come here.

39:49.178 --> 39:50.262
How clever.

39:53.724 --> 39:55.309
You asked me before

39:56.018 --> 39:57.853
about where I'm headed, right?

39:59.480 --> 40:02.274
and the reason why I'm doing all this now.

40:04.443 --> 40:06.153
It's a long story,

40:08.406 --> 40:10.658
and there's really
nothing pleasant about it.

40:15.371 --> 40:16.288
Wanna hear?

40:18.791 --> 40:20.459
[Yeon-jin] There are
white and polar nights,

40:20.543 --> 40:23.295
and my life has been a white night so far.

40:25.381 --> 40:26.674
It's always been bright.

40:28.008 --> 40:30.010
Yeah, of course.

40:32.138 --> 40:33.055
Why are you…?

40:33.139 --> 40:34.306
[door opens]

40:34.390 --> 40:35.433
[Ye-sol] Wow!

40:37.143 --> 40:38.644
Are you going to a party, Mom?

40:38.727 --> 40:40.771
She's actually going to work.

40:40.855 --> 40:43.357
A super famous fashion awards ceremony.

40:43.441 --> 40:45.025
Wow, that's cool!

40:45.734 --> 40:46.569
Hmm?

40:46.652 --> 40:47.528
[Yeon-jin chuckles]

40:47.611 --> 40:50.614
[Ye-sol] I can't wait to be
just like Mom when I grow up.

40:50.698 --> 40:53.701
I'm going to wear
all the pretty necklaces like she does,

40:53.784 --> 40:55.619
and a bunch of pretty dresses too!

40:55.703 --> 40:57.705
[solem choral music playing]

41:01.584 --> 41:03.127
I want to try this one.

41:03.210 --> 41:04.462
It's so pretty.

41:06.130 --> 41:07.131
[Yeon-jin chuckling]

41:09.508 --> 41:10.968
[Ye-sol] Oh, it's heavy.

41:11.051 --> 41:11.886
Hmm.

41:11.969 --> 41:14.680
Expensive jewelry, expensive watches,

41:14.763 --> 41:18.350
and expensive cars
and handbags are all heavy, you know?

41:19.185 --> 41:22.271
And expensive coats and dresses,

41:22.354 --> 41:23.606
expensive heels,

41:24.940 --> 41:25.941
are all light.

41:26.567 --> 41:27.401
You got it?

41:27.985 --> 41:29.069
I got it, Mom!

41:31.947 --> 41:32.948
Don't worry, Ye-sol.

41:35.701 --> 41:38.871
I'm not going to sink
below the horizon into a polar night…

41:43.209 --> 41:44.752
no matter what happens.

41:52.843 --> 41:53.844
[wry chuckle]

41:54.345 --> 41:55.763
TEST RESULTS
NAME: JEON JAE-JUN

41:55.846 --> 41:57.348
PROBABILITY OF PATERNITY: 99.999%

41:57.932 --> 41:58.933
No wonder.

42:01.101 --> 42:02.645
That's why she's so cute.

42:03.229 --> 42:04.230
[laughs]

42:16.492 --> 42:18.494
[dark string music playing]

42:18.911 --> 42:20.371
HA YE-SOL

42:22.289 --> 42:23.123
Excuse me.

42:23.874 --> 42:25.084
-Hello, Hye-jeong.
-Mmm.

42:25.584 --> 42:28.003
Someone from Information
left you something.

42:29.004 --> 42:31.215
-Did they find my phone?
-It's pretty thin.

42:31.298 --> 42:33.259
I don't think it's a phone. Here it is.

42:33.759 --> 42:35.553
-It was a rush delivery.
-[Hye-jeong] What?

42:53.779 --> 42:56.115
[breathing heavily]

43:24.393 --> 43:25.936
[footsteps clacking]

43:28.606 --> 43:30.274
[Dong-eun] I'm betting my whole life

43:31.150 --> 43:33.444
on getting revenge on all those people.

43:41.827 --> 43:42.828
[exhales shakily]

43:45.372 --> 43:48.667
So, you're not going… to stop?

43:50.377 --> 43:52.963
You're a better person
than those people, Dong-eun.

43:55.758 --> 43:56.967
I don't care about that.

43:58.677 --> 44:00.095
I get worse every day.

44:00.179 --> 44:01.972
Once you get your revenge,

44:03.682 --> 44:05.142
you will be ruined as well.

44:06.602 --> 44:08.437
[laughing]

44:16.236 --> 44:18.322
[continues laughing]

44:24.536 --> 44:26.080
I'm jealous of you, Yeo-jeong.

44:26.789 --> 44:29.333
Because your childhood
must have been sweet.

44:29.416 --> 44:31.585
You've grown up,
and you still have dignity.

44:32.544 --> 44:35.673
You can just go live your whole life
spouting cliches.

44:39.802 --> 44:41.595
Have you seen my scars before?

44:48.686 --> 44:49.687
Can you heal them?

44:58.821 --> 45:00.531
How long have you had these scars?

45:09.206 --> 45:10.958
Look at the face you're making now,

45:12.418 --> 45:13.919
after just seeing one arm.

45:15.421 --> 45:18.674
You still want me to stop this?

45:35.065 --> 45:37.067
[tender Korean pop ballad playing]

46:13.103 --> 46:14.938
[Dong-eun] There were
white nights sometimes,

46:16.148 --> 46:19.359
but most of my nights
felt like a polar night.

46:19.443 --> 46:21.445
[breathing shakily]

46:27.493 --> 46:28.494
They did this…

46:30.788 --> 46:31.789
to you?

46:34.291 --> 46:35.292
Did they?

46:36.460 --> 46:37.711
I'm already ruined.

46:38.504 --> 46:40.214
I have no dignity left.

46:41.423 --> 46:42.549
I need to do this.

46:44.176 --> 46:47.513
I want to stay faithful
to my rage and fury.

46:54.353 --> 46:55.354
[exhales shakily]

47:01.193 --> 47:02.110
I'll do it.

47:04.947 --> 47:06.532
I'll be your executioner.

47:10.702 --> 47:11.912
I'll join the hunt.

47:14.540 --> 47:15.707
Just tell me.

47:16.750 --> 47:18.043
What should I do first?

47:19.002 --> 47:20.170
What do you want next?

47:23.507 --> 47:24.508
Who can I…

47:27.469 --> 47:28.887
kill for you right now?

47:32.724 --> 47:34.726
[moody Korean pop song playing]

47:38.355 --> 47:40.357
[Korean pop song continuing]
